# Packaging does not happen here.
#
# `scripts/build.mjs` assembles a complete extension tree in dist/package/, and
# `npm run package` runs vsce there. That indirection exists because VS Code reads
# package.nls*.json only from the extension root: packaging from this directory would
# mean generating ten of them next to the source, which is what dist/ is for.
#
# Ignoring everything is deliberate. A stray `vsce package` run here would otherwise
# succeed and produce a vsix with no translations at all — a silent failure. As it stands
# such a run fails outright, and the reader ends up at this comment.
**
